[I] EDG C/C++ compiler

[T] The EDG C/C++ front end is the primary focus of this repository. The EDG
[T] front end is known for: its excellent parsing compatibility and bug
[T] emulation, to make sure source that compiles with Clang, GCC, and MSVC
[T] compiles with EDG; extensive documentation, to assist with development and
[T] modification; and extreme configurability, to allow it to be derived for
[T] use into a large number of C/C++ oriented products.
[T]
[T] The compiler project also includes: a C-generating back end, which can be
[T] used to generate C code for C++ programs; a C++-generating back end, which
[T] is useful for source-to-source transformation applications; a prelinker,
[T] which handles automatic template instantiation; a minimal runtime support
[T] library (but not any "real" libraries, e.g., for stream I/O); utilities to
[T] write the intermediate language to a file, read it back in, and display it
[T] in human-readable form; a name demangler; and a collection of purpose
[T] built development tools.

[U] https://github.com/edgcpp/compiler

[A] edgcpp
[M] andrei32 <andrei32.t2@gmail.com>

[C] extra/tool
[F] CROSS

[L] APL
[V] 7.0

[D] a87903f80749af2fa73c48d27f7b73c7ff1e1b76f7e93b2cd4895f29 compiler-7.0.tar.gz https://github.com/edgcpp/compiler/archive/7.0/

#posible: linux-{gcc,clang}-{debug,release}, macos-arm-clang-{debug,release}, windows-msvc-{debug,release}
var_append cmakeopt ' ' "--preset linux-gcc-release"

hook_add preconf 5 "export EDG_BASE="$builddir/compiler-$ver/bases/docker/dev-env/gcc""

hook_add premake 5 "cd build/gcc-release"

var_remove ninjaopt ' ' install
# for all targets $ninja -t targets | grep phony
var_append ninjaopt ' ' edg-cpp-rt-linux_x86_64

# it needs more files installed to run
hook_add postmake 5 "install -v bin/cpfe $root$bindir/"
